d></citation></ref><ref id="r11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal">Wentzel P, Gareskog M, Eriksson UJ: Folic acid supplementation diminishes diabetes- and glucose-induced dysmorphogenesis in rat embryos in vivo and in vitro. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>54</volume>: <fpage>546</fpage>&#x02013;553, <year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15677514</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Eriksson UJ, Sim&#x000e1;n CM: Pregnant diabetic rats fed the antioxidant butylated hydroxytoluene show decreased occurrence of malformations in the offspring. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>45</volume>: <fpage>1497</fpage>&#x02013;1502, <year>1996</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8866552</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Viana M, Herrera E, Bonet B: Teratogenic effects of diabetes mellitus in the rat. Prevention with vitamin E. <source>Diabetologia</source> <volume>39</volume>: <fpage>1041</fpage>&#x02013;1046, <year>1996</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8877287</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Sivan E, Reece EA, Wu YK, Homko CJ, Polansky M, Borenstein M: Dietary vitamin E prophylaxis and diabetic embryopathy: morphologic and biochemical analysis. <source>Am J Obstet Gynecol</source> <volume>175</volume>: <fpage>793</fpage>&#x02013;799, <year>1996</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8885724</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Sim&#x000e1;n CM, Eriksson UJ: Vitamin E decreases the occurrence of malformations in the offspring of diabetic rats. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>46</volume>: <fpage>1054</fpage>&#x02013;1061, <year>1997</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9166679</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Yang X, Borg LAH, Sim&#x000e1;n CM, Eriksson UJ: Maternal antioxidant treatments preven