Groot AC: Exposure of neural crest cells to elevated glucose leads to congenital heart defects, an effect that can be prevented by N-acetylcysteine. <source>Birth Defects Res A Clin Mol Teratol</source> <volume>79</volume>: <fpage>231</fpage>&#x02013;235, <year>2007</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17183584</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal">Wentzel P, Welsh N, Eriksson UJ: Developmental damage, increased lipid peroxidation, diminished cyclooxygenase-2 gene expression, and lowered PGE2 levels in rat embryos exposed to a diabetic environment. <source>Diabetes</source> <volume>48</volume>: <fpage>813</fpage>&#x02013;820, <year>1999</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10102698</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal">Wentzel P, Eriksson UJ: 8-Iso-PGF(2alpha) administration generates dysmorphogenesis and increased lipid peroxidation in rat embryos in vitro. <source>Teratology</source> <volume>66</volume>: <fpage>164</fpage>&#x02013;168, <year>2002</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12353212</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Cederberg J, Basu S, Eriksson UJ: Increased rate of lipid peroxidation and protein carbonylation in experimental diabetic pregnancy. <source>Diabetologia</source> <volume>44</volume>: <fpage>766</fpage>&#x02013;774, <year>2001</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11440370</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal">Styrud J, Thunberg L, Nybacka O, Eriksson UJ: Correlations between maternal metabolism and deranged development in the offspring of normal and diabetic rats. <source>Pediatr Res</source> <volume>37</volume>: <fpage>343</fpage>&#x02013;353, <year>1995</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7784144</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="r26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal">Fine EL, Horal M, Chang TI, Fortin G, Loeken MR: Evidence that eleva