op">15.8 &#x000b1; 1.2<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="t2fn1">&#x0002a;</xref><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="t2fn2">&#x02020;</xref></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Data are means &#x000b1; SE. The N and MD offspring are also subdivided into nonmalformed (N/MD normal) and malformed (N/MD malformed).</p></fn><fn id="t2fn1"><label>&#x0002a;</label><p><italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05 vs. N and</p></fn><fn id="t2fn2"><label>&#x02020;</label><p><italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05 vs. N/MD normal (Student's <italic>t</italic> test).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>